# Restore-point repository: source and settings only.
# Everything below is either huge, regenerated automatically, or both.

.venv/
cache/
backups/
catalog.json
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.tmp

# Packaging output. build/ is intermediate, dist/ holds the 65 MB installer; both are
# rebuilt from source by packaging/build.py and neither belongs in a restore-point repo.
build/
dist/

# The launcher's own log (Phase 26), rotated: launcher.log, launcher.log.1, launcher.log.2.
launcher.log*

# Copies of games' saves (Phase 29): the user's own data, rotated, and far too big for a
# restore-point repository.
save_backups/

# What the safety nets measured on this machine (Phase 39): the library the scanner found
# and a fingerprint of the original launcher folder. Machine-specific, and regenerated.
tests/baseline/

# The database prototype (8 October): its report names games as their folders on disk do.
docs/prototip-bd/report.md
# The database build.py writes when run as its README shows; rebuilt from data/ any time.
docs/prototip-bd/*.db

# The library database (Phase 67 on): the user's own data, like catalog.json never
# committed -- backups/ protects it -- and its rollback journal, there only mid-write.
library.db
library.db-journal
# The JSON the migration moved aside (Phase 69): the user's own records, never committed;
# and the database while it is built, refused, or being put back from a snapshot.
migrated/
library.db.building
library.db.refused
library.db.restoring
# A copy of the library kept as a phase's undo for the data, as its tag is for the code
# (Phase 93 on: library.before-phase-93.db, before a schema change).
/data/library.before-*.db
# The user's own settings and records, no longer tracked (Phase 69, the user's yes): the
# library lives in data/library.db (ignored above) and backups/ protects it; config.json
# holds the SteamGridDB key. Their old versions stay in the history -- the repository shown
# to the committee is a fresh export (docs/BAZA_DE_DATE.md, section 17).
/data/config.json
/data/overrides.json

# The Windows Sandbox file (Phase 78) names absolute paths on this PC; make_sandbox.py writes it.
packaging/sandbox/*.wsb

# Friends' anonymous exports and the comparison made from them (Phase 81): their data, never
# committed, even anonymous.
/data/exports/

# Launch videos made with the /brag plugin: renders and their working frames, not source.
/brag-output*/
# A copy of brag-output/brag.mp4 kept at the root.
/brag.mp4
